Consuming from the reagent vault without putting the materials in a bag
first. Retires the movement half of 0011; keeps the vault connected to
the engine's reagent machinery.

Touches: src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp -- Spell::CheckItems() (the
Reagent[] gate) and Spell::TakeReagents() (consumption), plus the
SPELL_FAILED_REAGENTS branch of Spell::WriteCastResultInfo() so the
"missing reagent" name uses the same arithmetic as the gate.

Why: the reagent bank is a STORE the player deliberately files materials
and tools into. Craft-from-vault was implemented (0011) by topping the
bag up -- withdrawing the shortfall into the backpack right before the
engine's HasItemCount check -- and normal consumption then destroyed it
from the bag. The observable behaviour was exactly what players
complained about: craft anything a few times and the vault was drained
into the backpack, tools included in the pre-0022 era, materials always.
Any craft whose later checks failed (or a craft-all batch cancelled
halfway) left the topped-up reagents stranded in the bags with no
command to send them back except DEPOSITALL.

The fix is the same shape 0022 already used for tools: ANSWER the check
in place instead of moving anything.

  Spell::CheckItems, the Reagent[] check
-                LivingGear_TopUpReagentFromVault(player, itemid, itemcount);
-                if (!player->HasItemCount(itemid, itemcount, true))
+                if (!player->HasItemCount(itemid, itemcount, true)
+                    && !LivingGear_VaultCoversReagent(player, itemid, itemcount))
                     return SPELL_FAILED_REAGENTS;

  Spell::TakeReagents, the consumption loop
-        p_caster->DestroyItemCount(itemid, itemcount, true);
+        LivingGear_ConsumeReagent(p_caster, itemid, itemcount);

LivingGear_VaultCoversReagent (LivingGear_Vault.cpp) returns true when
bags + bank + vault cover the requirement. LivingGear_ConsumeReagent
pays from bags/bank via the normal DestroyItemCount bookkeeping and
burns only the shortfall directly out of the vault (VaultRemove), then
sends the VLT| sync line so the client's vault panel and craftable
totals stay fresh mid-batch -- the stale-count lesson from 2026-08-24,
kept.

Nothing else changes. Tools still satisfy Totem[]/TotemCategory[] in
place via 0022 and are never consumed. The client addon's CRAFTPREP
staging request and its watchdog/fallback machinery are removed at the
same time -- their only job was to stage materials into the bag for a
cast the client might refuse, and no such cast exists: the Create
button already counts the vault (GetTradeSkillInfo / GetCraftInfo /
GetTradeSkillReagentInfo / GetCraftReagentInfo hooks), so a refused
craft is now refused for a real reason instead of being papered over
with a quiet withdrawal.

--- a/src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp
@@ near the other Living Gear forward declarations
-void LivingGear_TopUpReagentFromVault(Player* player, uint32 itemId, uint32 needed);
+bool LivingGear_VaultCoversReagent(Player* player, uint32 itemId, uint32 needed);
+void LivingGear_ConsumeReagent(Player* player, uint32 itemId, uint32 count);

@@ Spell::CheckItems, the MAX_SPELL_REAGENTS loop
-                LivingGear_TopUpReagentFromVault(player, itemid, itemcount);
-                if (!player->HasItemCount(itemid, itemcount, true))
+                if (!player->HasItemCount(itemid, itemcount, true)
+                    && !LivingGear_VaultCoversReagent(player, itemid, itemcount))
                     return SPELL_FAILED_REAGENTS;

@@ Spell::TakeReagents, the consumption loop
-        p_caster->DestroyItemCount(itemid, itemcount, true);
+        LivingGear_ConsumeReagent(p_caster, itemid, itemcount);

@@ Spell::WriteCastResultInfo, SPELL_FAILED_REAGENTS
-                    if (!caster->HasItemCount(itemid, itemcount))
+                    if (!caster->HasItemCount(itemid, itemcount)
+                        && !LivingGear_VaultCoversReagent(caster, itemid, itemcount))
